<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tarchon</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tarchon was a legendary Etruscan hero, said in ancient tradition to have founded Tarquinii and other cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruria">Etruria</a>. Some versions make him the brother or son of Tyrrhenus, who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruscans">Etruscans</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydia">Lydia</a>, and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virgil">Virgil</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aeneid">Aeneid</a> he commands the Etruscans as an ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aeneas">Aeneas</a>. In the legend of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tages">Tages</a> he is the ploughman who received the prophet's teachings.</p></div>
